🚀 Week 2 – Day 3 Static vs Instance Methods in Java ☕

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧠 Introduction

In Java, methods are mainly of two types:

✔ Static Methods
✔ Instance Methods

👉 Understanding their difference is **very important for interviews & OOP concepts 🔥**

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

⚡ 1. Static Methods

A static method belongs to the **class**, not to objects.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 Characteristics

✔ Declared using `static` keyword
✔ Can be called without object
✔ Shared among all objects

---

📌 Example

```java id="s1"
class Demo {

    static void display() {
        System.out.println("Static Method");
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        display();
    }
}
```

---

🔍 Important Points

✔ Memory allocated once
✔ Can access only static members directly
✔ Faster because no object creation needed

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

⚡ 2. Instance Methods

An instance method belongs to an **object**.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 Characteristics

✔ No `static` keyword
✔ Requires object creation
✔ Each object can use method

---

📌 Example

```java id="s2"
class Demo {

    void show() {
        System.out.println("Instance Method");
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Demo obj = new Demo();
        obj.show();
    }
}
```

---

🔍 Important Points

✔ Can access both static & instance members
✔ Requires memory for objects

---

📊 Static vs Instance Methods

| Feature              | Static Method | Instance Method |
| -------------------- | ------------- | --------------- |
| Belongs To           | Class         | Object          |
| Object Required      | ❌ No          | ✔ Yes         |
| Keyword              | `static`      | No keyword      |
| Memory Allocation    | Once          | Per object      |
| Access Instance Data | ❌ Directly No | ✔ Yes         |

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔁 Calling Techniques

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 Static Method Calling

```java id="s3"
Demo.display();
```

OR

```java id="s4"
display();
```

---

🔹 Instance Method Calling

```java id="s5"
Demo obj = new Demo();
obj.show();
```

---

⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Calling instance method without object
❌ Accessing non-static variables inside static method
❌ Confusing class methods with object methods

---

📌 Example Error

```java id="s6"
class Test {

    int x = 10;

    static void show() {
        System.out.println(x); // Error
    }
}
```

👉 Static methods cannot directly access instance variables ❌

---

🎯 When to Use What?

🔹 Use Static Methods When:

✔ Method logic is common for all objects
✔ No object-specific data needed

Examples:

* `Math.sqrt()`
* Utility methods

---

🔹 Use Instance Methods When:

✔ Method depends on object data
✔ Behavior changes for different objects

Examples:

* Bank account operations
* Student details

---

🧠 Real Insight

👉 Most utility/helper methods are static.

👉 Real-world applications mainly use instance methods because they work with object data.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📚 Key Takeaways

✔ Static methods belong to class
✔ Instance methods belong to objects
✔ Static methods don’t require objects
✔ Instance methods require object creation
✔ Static methods cannot directly access instance data

